  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "The proposal is for a roof extension, rear extension, and some changes to\nthe façades. The roof extension has been set back from the front façade\nto reflect the existing roof layout, and the rear extension is proposed to\nmeet the height of the existing garden wall to no. 61. Bin, bike, and ASHP\nstorage are also proposed at the existing front garden level.\n\nThe design incorporates the materiality and detailing of the existing\nhouse, updating all surfaces to a higher standard throughout. This\nensures longevity for modern family use. The extensions have been\ndesigned to minimise any adverse effect on neighbouring properties’\ndaylight levels and adhere to the principles of the permitted development\nguidelines.\n\nThe proposal includes improvements in the building’s energy efficiency\nwith triple glazing, new insulation on all external walls, floors, roofs, and\nan ASHP to power the heating and hot water.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed roof extension by reason of its location on a terrace of properties with an unimpaired roofline, and its detailed design, would be detrimental to the character and appearance of the building, the terrace as a whole and the general street scene contrary to the requirements of policy D1 (Design) of the Camden Local Plan 2017. ",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed rear extension, by reason of its scale, siting and design, would fail to be subservient to the host building and would be detrimental to the character and appearance of the host property contrary to the requirements of policy D1 (Design) of the Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed front boundary fence and gates, due to their height and location, would be detrimental to the character and appearance of the host property and street scene contrary to the requirements of policy D1 (Design) of the Camden Local Plan 2017.\r\n"
  ],
